
# 3. TRD — TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT

# FixMyCampus — Technical Requirements Document

**Version:** 1.0
**Date:** 06 September 2026

---

# 1. Technical Overview

FixMyCampus is a browser-based web application consisting of:

```text
HTML/CSS/JavaScript
        ↓
PHP Backend
        ↓
MySQL Database
```

XML, XSD, and DTD are used for complaint data export and validation.

---

# 2. Technology Environment

| Component           | Technology              |
| ------------------- | ----------------------- |
| OS                  | Windows                 |
| Web Server          | Apache                  |
| Server Package      | XAMPP                   |
| Frontend            | HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript |
| Backend             | PHP                     |
| Database            | MySQL 9.7.1             |
| Database Port       | 3306                    |
| Data Format         | XML                     |
| Schema              | XSD                     |
| Document Definition | DTD                     |

---

# 3. Application Architecture

The system follows a layered architecture.

### Presentation Layer

Contains:

* HTML
* CSS
* JavaScript

Responsible for:

* User interface
* Forms
* Dashboards
* Tables
* Chat
* Notifications

### Application Layer

Contains PHP endpoints.

Responsible for:

* Authentication
* Authorization
* Validation
* Complaint processing
* Assignment
* Status changes
* Chat
* Notifications
* Feedback

### Persistence Layer

MySQL stores:

* Users
* Complaints
* Assignments
* Updates
* Messages
* Notifications
* Feedback

### XML Layer

Responsible for:

* XML generation
* XSD validation
* DTD validation

---

# 4. Database Design

| Table             | Purpose                                     |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| users             | Stores users and authentication information |
| categories        | Stores complaint categories                 |
| locations         | Stores campus locations                     |
| complaints        | Stores complaints                           |
| complaint_updates | Stores status history                       |
| staff_assignments | Stores staff assignment information         |
| messages          | Stores complaint chat                       |
| notifications     | Stores notifications                        |
| feedback          | Stores post-closure feedback                |

---

# 5. Database Relationships

The main relationships are:

```text
users
  │
  ├── complaints
  │
  ├── complaint_updates
  │
  ├── staff_assignments
  │
  ├── messages
  │
  ├── notifications
  │
  └── feedback

categories
      │
      └── complaints

locations
      │
      └── complaints

complaints
      │
      ├── complaint_updates
      ├── staff_assignments
      ├── messages
      ├── notifications
      └── feedback
```

